{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00280",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Good afternoon. Have a seat and we'll begin. Weather's turned, hasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.23,
      "end_seconds": 10.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "It has. I got caught in the rain walking over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.73,
      "end_seconds": 13.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Tell me from the beginning, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.75,
      "end_seconds": 20.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "I've been dealing with diarrhoea. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.83,
      "end_seconds": 25.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Alright, is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.05,
      "end_seconds": 32.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "It's been going on for about four days. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.38,
      "end_seconds": 43.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.69,
      "end_seconds": 55.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "Hmm, maybe a four out of ten on a bad day. It's once or twice a day. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.36,
      "end_seconds": 69.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.45,
      "end_seconds": 73.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.58,
      "end_seconds": 76.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Have you had any rash, weight loss or recent antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.27,
      "end_seconds": 83.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Uh, I haven't had rash, weight loss or recent antibiotics, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.06,
      "end_seconds": 96.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.62,
      "end_seconds": 99.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.57,
      "end_seconds": 107.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.87,
      "end_seconds": 112.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Latex. I come out in... well, a rash on my hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.26,
      "end_seconds": 117.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.23,
      "end_seconds": 122.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.52,
      "end_seconds": 130.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "No, nothing, I've generally been healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.05,
      "end_seconds": 134.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "So, one moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.88,
      "end_seconds": 135.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.05,
      "end_seconds": 154.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.24,
      "end_seconds": 158.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "It's ORS, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.86,
      "end_seconds": 163.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.71,
      "end_seconds": 164.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.36,
      "end_seconds": 194.16,
      "duration_seconds": 16.8,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.46,
      "end_seconds": 197.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.27,
      "end_seconds": 202.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.48,
      "end_seconds": 203.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.05,
      "end_seconds": 222.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. From what you've told me, this looks most like acute gastroenteritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.13,
      "end_seconds": 227.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.48,
      "end_seconds": 246.59,
      "duration_seconds": 15.11,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now acute gastroenteritis is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had diarrhoea for about four days, and no rash or recent antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.06,
      "end_seconds": 250.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.63,
      "end_seconds": 252.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.27,
      "end_seconds": 255.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.06,
      "end_seconds": 272.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. I'm going to order blood salts, for dehydration. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.54,
      "end_seconds": 276.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.71,
      "end_seconds": 288.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "I'm prescribing zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day, for ten days. That should help with diarrhoea. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.49,
      "end_seconds": 290.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.9,
      "end_seconds": 310.71,
      "duration_seconds": 19.81,
      "text": "Stick to bananas, rice, toast, curd, and avoid milk and oily food till it settles. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Please don't sit on it if you pass blood or can't keep anything down. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.24,
      "end_seconds": 313.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.3,
      "end_seconds": 317.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Please come and see me in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.78,
      "end_seconds": 321.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.0,
      "end_seconds": 329.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.5,
      "end_seconds": 338.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "So, I take the zinc, 20 milligrams, once a day and come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.2,
      "end_seconds": 343.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.09,
      "end_seconds": 346.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.38,
      "end_seconds": 348.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}